IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`

-- Section 8: Certain monetary amounts to be construed in fee units or penalty units.
-- Each subsection says that a provision "may be construed as authorising" a rule or instrument to be made by reference to a unit.
-- That is a permission to construe, limited in its own words to the provisions it describes: a provision inside the description may be so construed;
-- for a provision outside it the text says neither yes nor no, so the answer is NOTHING.

§ `Section 8 -- Certain monetary amounts to be construed in fee units or penalty units`

-- src:80 | (1) A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule to prescribe, fix or charge that fee by reference to a fee unit.
@ref s 8(1) (src:80)
GIVEN `the provision is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statutory rule prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` MEANS
    IF     `the provision is in an Act`
       AND `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule`
       AND `the statutory rule prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "A provision in an Act or a statutory rule": the kind of instrument that holds the provision is asked, and an Act or a statutory rule is within the subsection.
-- src:82 | (1A) A provision in an Act or a statutory rule authorising an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the instrument maker to make a legislative instrument to prescribe, fix or charge that fee by reference to a fee unit.
@ref s 8(1A) (src:82)
GIVEN `the instrument that holds the provision` IS AN Instrument
      `the provision authorises an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislative instrument prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` MEANS
    IF     `the instrument that holds the provision is an Act or a statutory rule`
       AND `the provision authorises an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument`
       AND `the legislative instrument prescribes, fixes or charges a fee, however expressed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the instrument that holds the provision is an Act or a statutory rule` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the instrument that holds the provision`
            WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a statutory rule` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- src:83 | (2) A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule to prescribe that penalty by reference to a penalty unit.
@ref s 8(2) (src:83)
GIVEN `the provision is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statutory rule prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule, however expressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the penalty by reference to a penalty unit` MEANS
    IF     `the provision is in an Act`
       AND `the provision authorises the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule`
       AND `the statutory rule prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule, however expressed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
